@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Deploying Applications to Azure";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to efficiently deploy applications to Microsoft Azure using best practices, automation, and Azure DevOps.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>
            Deploying applications to Azure involves leveraging cloud infrastructure to ensure scalability, high availability, and security. 
            Azure provides various deployment options, including Azure App Services, Virtual Machines, Kubernetes Service (AKS), and Function Apps.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="~/css/images/AzureDevOps/azure-deployment.png" alt="Azure Deployment" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg" />
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure provides flexible deployment options.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Deployment Methods -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Azure Deployment Methods</h2>
        <p>Azure supports multiple ways to deploy applications, depending on the architecture and use case:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Azure App Services:</strong> Ideal for hosting web apps, APIs, and mobile backends.</li>
            <li><strong>Azure Virtual Machines (VMs):</strong> Full control over the OS and environment.</li>
            <li><strong>Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS):</strong> Containerized applications with orchestration.</li>
            <li><strong>Azure Functions:</strong> Serverless computing for event-driven applications.</li>
            <li><strong>Azure Logic Apps:</strong> Workflow automation without writing code.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Deployment with Azure DevOps -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Deploying with Azure DevOps</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps provides a seamless way to automate deployments through CI/CD pipelines. Steps include:
        </p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Set up a repository:</strong> Store your application code in Azure Repos or GitHub.</li>
            <li><strong>Build pipeline:</strong> Create a pipeline to compile, test, and package the application.</li>
            <li><strong>Release pipeline:</strong> Automate deployments to different environments (Dev, Test, Prod).</li>
            <li><strong>Infrastructure as Code (IaC):</strong> Use ARM templates or Terraform for resource provisioning.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitoring & Logging:</strong> Use Azure Monitor and Application Insights for tracking performance.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices for Azure Deployment</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Use <strong>blue-green deployment</strong> or <strong>canary releases</strong> to minimize downtime.</li>
            <li>Ensure <strong>high availability</strong> with load balancers and traffic management.</li>
            <li>Implement <strong>role-based access control (RBAC)</strong> for secure deployments.</li>
            <li>Automate <strong>infrastructure provisioning</strong> using ARM or Terraform.</li>
            <li>Monitor deployments using <strong>Azure Monitor</strong> and set up alerts.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Deploying applications to Azure enables organizations to scale and manage workloads efficiently. 
            By leveraging Azure DevOps and automation, deployments can be streamlined, secure, and highly available.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="~/css/images/AzureDevOps/azure-devops-pipeline.png" alt="Azure DevOps Deployment Pipeline" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg" />
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>End-to-end CI/CD pipeline with Azure DevOps.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>